1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:05,130
[wind howling]

2
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:22,820
[baby crying]

3
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:29,110
[YAMAHA] There's another child
inside you!

4
00:00:29,150 --> 00:00:31,910
-It's truly happening... twins!
-[Nagisa grunting]

5
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:34,490
You've nearly made it to dawn!

6
00:00:34,530 --> 00:00:36,790
You must resist
the urge to push!

7
00:00:36,830 --> 00:00:40,120
Resist? You know you're asking
the impossible, Granny!

8
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:41,290
[YAMAHA]
That doesn't matter!

9
00:00:41,330 --> 00:00:42,460
[Nagisa groaning]

10
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,630
Even if it's impossible,
she must.

11
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:47,300
If she does this,

12
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:49,010
her children will be the ones

13
00:00:49,050 --> 00:00:51,760
to place the Daemons
under their command!

14
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:53,220
♪

15
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:02,850
[babies crying]

16
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:14,910
[babies continue crying]

17
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:16,660
[Mine grunts softly]

18
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,330
[MINE] The children who sunder
night and day

19
00:01:20,370 --> 00:01:22,290
have been born to us.

20
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:24,880
♪

21
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:31,930
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

22
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:37,180
16 YEARS LATER

23
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:39,930
[birds calling]

24
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:16,590
[thuds]

25
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:18,890
[footsteps]

26
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:26,900
[plane flying overhead]

27
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,950
[YURU] Perfect trails
of dragon wind.

28
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:38,120
EPISODE 1
"ASA AND YURU"

29
00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:52,840
[Danji groans]

30
00:02:54,470 --> 00:02:56,630
[DANJI] Hm? [chuckles]

31
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:59,680
Hey, Yuru, don't tell me.

32
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:02,180
Did you go hunting
by yourself again?

33
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:04,430
[YURU] Hey, Danji,
just got back.

34
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:06,060
[DANJI] You know
I would've gone with

35
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:07,980
-if you would've asked!
-Sorry.

36
00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:09,650
What if something happened
in the mountains

37
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:11,400
while you were
by yourself, huh?

38
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:12,860
What would you have done?

39
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:14,780
[YURU] It's fine, really.

40
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:18,740
I trust the Left and the Right
to protect me.

41
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:21,370
[Danji laughs] Wow!

42
00:03:21,410 --> 00:03:23,200
You nabbed yourself a pheasant?

43
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,410
That must've been hard!

44
00:03:24,710 --> 00:03:25,790
[YURU] Not really.

45
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,750
We're havin' roast pheasant
tonight! [chuckles]

46
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:29,540
-[YURU] Stewed.
-[DANJI] No way.

47
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:31,380
Roast pheasant smells
and tastes way better.

48
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:32,710
[YURU] Stew will make you
feel full longer.

49
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:34,170
[DANJI] Ah, who cares?

50
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:36,970
Hey, Yuru, welcome back.

51
00:03:37,010 --> 00:03:38,300
Get ready.

52
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:39,970
We're in for bad weather
tonight.

53
00:03:40,010 --> 00:03:42,970
[sighs] That's fine by me
as long as it means rain.

54
00:03:43,010 --> 00:03:45,180
Do you want some help later?

55
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:46,690
Sure! Thanks, kid!

56
00:03:46,730 --> 00:03:48,560
♪

57
00:03:52,730 --> 00:03:55,740
[BOY] Huh? Oh! [chuckles]

58
00:03:55,990 --> 00:03:57,320
[BOY] Hey!

59
00:03:58,320 --> 00:03:59,780
[man chuckles]

60
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:00,950
[Kyoka grunting]

61
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:03,120
[Kyoka sighs]

62
00:04:03,330 --> 00:04:05,370
[YURU] Granny Yamaha, I'm back.

63
00:04:05,410 --> 00:04:07,250
You look well, Yuru.

64
00:04:07,290 --> 00:04:09,620
Danji, your timing
couldn't be better!

65
00:04:09,670 --> 00:04:11,500
[Danji exclaims] But Mom!

66
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:13,340
Stop your whining!

67
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:14,960
[DANJI] Look at that. Gotta go!

68
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,090
Come back!

69
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:18,630
Why can't you be
more diligent like Yuru?

70
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:20,470
Granny, how's Asa?

71
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:23,060
Good. That sister of yours
has been working

72
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:24,760
since you left for the hunt.

73
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:41,620
[YURU] Asa...

74
00:04:42,990 --> 00:04:44,240
How are you?

75
00:04:46,490 --> 00:04:49,870
Big brother, welcome back home!

76
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,500
[Yuru chuckles]

77
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:53,580
♪

78
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:55,290
[YURU] I caught
a pheasant today.

79
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:57,630
That's so impressive!

80
00:04:57,670 --> 00:04:59,300
It's really not.

81
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:02,550
I was hoping to catch a boar
or a deer instead.

82
00:05:02,590 --> 00:05:04,050
It's been so dry all year.

83
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:06,010
I'm worried the crops might die.

84
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:09,520
If that happens, food will be
scarce for the winter.

85
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,810
I need to hunt more,

86
00:05:10,850 --> 00:05:13,770
then preserve it with salt,
or make jerky.

87
00:05:14,190 --> 00:05:16,770
[ASA] If the harvest
does wind up that bad,

88
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,690
will the adults have
to go down the mountain

89
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:19,690
to find work?

90
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:21,280
It's possible.

91
00:05:22,490 --> 00:05:24,620
[ASA] Will you be leaving
to join them?

92
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:26,120
Not a chance!

93
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:28,330
Look, why do you think I've been
putting in so much time

94
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:29,910
to get better at hunting?

95
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:32,750
I'd do anything to keep
from going down the mountain,

96
00:05:32,790 --> 00:05:35,750
so I'll just make myself
too valuable to send away.

97
00:05:35,790 --> 00:05:37,960
You promise you're not gonna
leave me alone?

98
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,840
You won't abandon us
the same way our parents did?

99
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:43,050
You do not need to worry, Asa.

100
00:05:43,090 --> 00:05:45,640
I swear I'll protect you
for as long as I live.

101
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:47,720
I am never going to leave
this village!

102
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:49,270
Not while you're here!

103
00:05:49,310 --> 00:05:51,060
The two of us
will stick together!

104
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,350
[ASA)] Huh?

105
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:55,690
[chuckles] Always!

106
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:58,360
-[Yuru chuckles]
-[KYOKA] Yuru.

107
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:00,320
What's wrong?

108
00:06:00,650 --> 00:06:01,940
[KYOKA] Mm...

109
00:06:01,990 --> 00:06:03,990
Nothing. Dera's here.

110
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,160
♪

111
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:07,120
[MAN] This is some good steel.

112
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:10,160
[DERA] These are from the guys
who just left.

113
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:12,120
[MAN]
Thanks for always doing this.

114
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:14,000
How is it down there, anyway?

115
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:16,630
There's been a nasty illness
going around.

116
00:06:16,670 --> 00:06:18,550
Our luck. Yeah?

117
00:06:18,590 --> 00:06:21,960
Hear that? Means I'll be buying
medicinal herbs at a premium!

118
00:06:22,010 --> 00:06:23,930
I'll trade these for some salt.

119
00:06:23,970 --> 00:06:26,510
Got any seeds for veggies
that don't need much rain?

120
00:06:27,010 --> 00:06:28,560
[DERA] But of course.

121
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:31,310
Excuse me,
my girl's turning seven soon.

122
00:06:31,350 --> 00:06:32,520
[DERA] Time sure flies!

123
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:34,890
I'll bring a shaman with me
on my next trip!

124
00:06:34,940 --> 00:06:36,440
[BOTH] Mm... [chuckling]

125
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:39,230
My headaches
have been getting worse.

126
00:06:39,730 --> 00:06:41,190
Your usual painkillers?

127
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,690
[indistinct chatter]

128
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,440
-[DERA] On it!
-[YURU] Uh?

129
00:06:44,490 --> 00:06:45,490
Dera!

130
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:48,120
Hey, Yuru! How ya been?

131
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:49,910
Anything
you're lookin' for today?

132
00:06:50,290 --> 00:06:52,870
Well, there's nothing
that I need. Uh...

133
00:06:52,910 --> 00:06:55,000
"My sister on the other hand.

134
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:57,540
I'll take anything you've got!"
Right?

135
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:59,960
-[YURU] Hmm.
-[indistinct chatter]

136
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,920
It's perfect.

137
00:07:02,210 --> 00:07:04,420
[DERA] What? You've got
pheasant feathers?

138
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:07,180
Look at you!
Those sell for a fortune!

139
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:12,470
[DANJI] He's so lucky.

140
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:15,690
I wish I could leave
the village for a day.

141
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:18,730
[YURU] What, do you think
it's nice? Out there?

142
00:07:18,770 --> 00:07:20,770
Consider all the people
who left us.

143
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:23,400
We rarely see them come back
to this boring place.

144
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:26,240
It must be way better
than being a peasant. Like me!

145
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,120
I'm not so sure.

146
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:31,660
I wouldn't mind living
in this village my whole life.

147
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:34,120
[DANJI] Easy for you to say.

148
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:37,500
You've got a cute little sister
to keep you company.

149
00:07:37,870 --> 00:07:40,630
Why don't you just take her
and get out of this life?

150
00:07:40,670 --> 00:07:43,670
I'll be happy to come along,
if that'd make you feel safer.

151
00:07:43,710 --> 00:07:46,670
I can't have you hanging
around Asa. You'd corrupt her.

152
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:48,510
[exclaims] What'd you say?

153
00:07:48,550 --> 00:07:51,310
Asa has an important job here!
You got it?

154
00:07:51,350 --> 00:07:53,890
Great! But if no one
can actually see her,

155
00:07:53,930 --> 00:07:56,100
how do we know
she's not imaginary?

156
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:58,140
Only a select few may visit her.

157
00:07:58,190 --> 00:08:01,020
Aren't I "select" enough,
big brother?

158
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:04,110
Sorry, but an oaf like you will
probably never get to meet her.

159
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:06,360
[Danji grunts]
Those are fightin' words!

160
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:07,950
[YURU] Fine, you can
see her if you win!

161
00:08:07,990 --> 00:08:10,370
[DANJI] Wait, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no!

162
00:08:10,410 --> 00:08:12,870
-[plane flying overhead]
-[DANJI] Uh?

163
00:08:13,290 --> 00:08:14,700
What's that sound?

164
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:17,160
I'm pretty sure
it's just another dragon.

165
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:18,500
-Look there.
-Uh?

166
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:21,460
[YURU] More trails
of dragon wind.

167
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:25,380
[helicopter whirring]

168
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:33,890
That roar is unusual.

169
00:08:33,930 --> 00:08:36,100
This one sounds almost rhythmic.

170
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:38,430
I've heard some like it
a few times before,

171
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:40,350
when I was hunting deep
in the mountains.

172
00:08:40,390 --> 00:08:42,730
It's pretty loud, though, right?

173
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:44,480
Maybe it's close.

174
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:47,070
Hey, man, have you ever
seen a dragon?

175
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:48,400
Never, no.

176
00:08:49,530 --> 00:08:51,320
♪

177
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:12,630
What's that thing?

178
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:20,230
[both gasp]

179
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:27,480
[helicopter whirring]

180
00:09:27,530 --> 00:09:28,900
[both gasp]

181
00:09:41,870 --> 00:09:42,920
[horse neighs]

182
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:49,920
-[both exclaim]
-[BOY] Hey!

183
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:52,050
[all gasp]

184
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:55,970
[muffled grunting]

185
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:05,860
[Dera gasping]

186
00:10:10,190 --> 00:10:12,490
[gunshots in distance]

187
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,910
Hey! So, Granny Yamaha,

188
00:10:18,950 --> 00:10:21,080
do you know
what's going on here?

189
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,330
It's the barrier.

190
00:10:22,370 --> 00:10:24,540
They managed
to destroy it somehow.

191
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:25,750
How'd they do that?

192
00:10:25,790 --> 00:10:27,790
I don't know.
But they're probably trying

193
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:29,420
-to abduct Yuru.
-Huh?

194
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:32,090
We have to hide him
somewhere safe right now!

195
00:10:32,130 --> 00:10:34,300
-Bring him straight away to me!
-Right!

196
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:35,840
[MAN 1] Where is he?

197
00:10:36,090 --> 00:10:38,350
[MAN 2] Most likely
in the fields below! Hurry!

198
00:10:41,810 --> 00:10:43,560
[DANJI] What's this?

199
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,560
What happened here?

200
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:46,980
[Danji breathes shakily]

201
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:50,440
They're all dead.
I don't understand.

202
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:53,450
-[YURU] Danji, stay close.
-[Danji grunts]

203
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:56,160
Please, Mom.
Please still be alive!

204
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:57,820
[Danji panting]

205
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:05,250
[Combatant 1 gasps]
That's the boy!

206
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:08,040
[COMBATANT 2]
Stand down.

207
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:12,630
[shrieks] What's that?
Something flew by super-fast!

208
00:11:12,670 --> 00:11:15,420
I don't know, but I don't think
you wanna get hit by one.

209
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:18,890
[combatants grunting]

210
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:21,430
[Danji panting]

211
00:11:21,470 --> 00:11:24,140
Looks like those dragons
made it over the outer wall!

212
00:11:24,730 --> 00:11:26,640
[YURU] I doubt
we could fight them.

213
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:29,110
Can you even call them dragons?

214
00:11:29,650 --> 00:11:31,610
[Danji panting]

215
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:38,700
Well, my mom's probably
around the keep,

216
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:40,120
same place as usual.

217
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:42,330
And I'm guessing you're
also headed there

218
00:11:42,370 --> 00:11:44,290
to find Asa? Huh?

219
00:11:44,330 --> 00:11:45,580
[YURU] Give me a hand.

220
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,210
[Danji grunts] With what?

221
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:49,420
-[YURU] Just trust me.
-Hm?

222
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:52,420
[Danji grunts]

223
00:11:57,300 --> 00:11:59,090
Whoa, what is this?

224
00:11:59,180 --> 00:12:00,600
[YURU] A shortcut to the keep.

225
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:02,760
That was here? All this time?

226
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:04,470
I had no clue!

227
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:05,770
Told you.

228
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:08,600
The Left and Right
will protect us.

229
00:12:09,230 --> 00:12:10,860
[ladder creaking]

230
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:15,320
Asa, stay safe.

231
00:12:15,780 --> 00:12:18,360
[grunts] Hey, Yuru!

232
00:12:28,210 --> 00:12:30,540
So how's it hangin', guys?

233
00:12:36,050 --> 00:12:37,470
Gobble.

234
00:12:38,170 --> 00:12:39,720
-[grunts]
-[villagers gasping]

235
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:45,680
-Gobble.
-[grunts]

236
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:48,140
-Gobbly-gob.
-[men grunting]

237
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:49,850
Gobble, gobble.

238
00:12:52,610 --> 00:12:53,940
You too.

239
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:58,450
[Azami whimpers]

240
00:13:04,490 --> 00:13:06,200
Mommy!

241
00:13:06,870 --> 00:13:09,250
It's fine, I don't bite kids!

242
00:13:09,290 --> 00:13:11,710
[man whimpering]

243
00:13:12,210 --> 00:13:13,790
Gobble.

244
00:13:14,130 --> 00:13:15,880
[Azami screams]

245
00:13:17,250 --> 00:13:19,510
What up? This is Gabby.

246
00:13:19,550 --> 00:13:22,510
The outer and middle zones
have been mostly emptied out.

247
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:27,010
Send the ground force,
we're all clear here.

248
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:32,980
[helicopter whirring]

249
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:35,060
Hey, is anyone listening?

250
00:13:36,150 --> 00:13:38,280
Oh, man, what a mess.

251
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:40,650
What to do about all this?

252
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:44,410
Can't believe they managed
to break the barrier.

253
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:49,120
Hey, hey. Hana?
We got a problem here.

254
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:52,330
Damn, even the signal's
getting through.

255
00:13:52,370 --> 00:13:53,630
This is bad.

256
00:13:53,670 --> 00:13:55,790
Can you see the smoke
from there?

257
00:13:56,290 --> 00:13:57,590
Great.

258
00:13:57,630 --> 00:14:00,550
Looks like we gotta change
the rendezvous point.

259
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:02,170
Yep.

260
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:03,800
I'm pretty sure...

261
00:14:04,550 --> 00:14:06,300
Asa's here.

262
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:21,110
Oh, yeah?

263
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:23,990
So that's the way it's gonna be.

264
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:26,160
[breathes nervously]

265
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,410
[ASA] Disgusting.

266
00:14:29,450 --> 00:14:30,910
[Asa gasps]

267
00:14:32,660 --> 00:14:33,910
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

268
00:14:35,710 --> 00:14:36,920
[ASA] Disgusting.

269
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,290
[Asa gasps]

270
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:41,380
[gasps]

271
00:14:56,890 --> 00:14:58,310
[Yuru gasps]

272
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:00,360
-[YURU] Asa!
-[ASA] Yes?

273
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,530
Your Asa is right here.

274
00:15:02,570 --> 00:15:03,990
I've come to save you.

275
00:15:04,030 --> 00:15:06,570
-[Yuru gasps softly]
-And after that...

276
00:15:06,870 --> 00:15:08,740
[Asa exhales sharply]

277
00:15:08,990 --> 00:15:11,030
...I'm gonna kill
everybody else.

278
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,450
[gasps] Hold on.

279
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:17,080
Whoever you are, you're lying.

280
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,090
You clearly aren't.

281
00:15:20,630 --> 00:15:22,800
[voice trembles] And she's...

282
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:26,550
You're not my sister! Drop dead!

283
00:15:26,590 --> 00:15:28,220
Get away from her!

284
00:15:34,270 --> 00:15:37,940
[DERA] They disguised themselves
as mountain rescue choppers.

285
00:15:38,610 --> 00:15:40,770
[gunshots]

286
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:49,030
[DERA] Gotta make sure
they can't follow me from above

287
00:15:49,070 --> 00:15:50,660
while I'm making my escape.

288
00:15:55,910 --> 00:15:57,210
Oh, man...

289
00:15:57,920 --> 00:15:59,580
My, my...

290
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,960
Well, little red,
what big teeth you have!

291
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,050
[Gabriel growls]

292
00:16:07,670 --> 00:16:10,760
Wow. You can see
my friends, mister?

293
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:14,600
[gunshots]

294
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:16,890
That enamel's hard as rocks!

295
00:16:16,930 --> 00:16:19,980
I take it you're the one
who killed our ground forces.

296
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:22,520
Huh?

297
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:24,480
[grunts]

298
00:16:32,490 --> 00:16:35,660
My bad. I was only trying
to break the arrow.

299
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:39,080
I'm still getting used to this.

300
00:16:54,390 --> 00:16:55,810
[Asa grunts]

301
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:59,980
Dera, take Yuru and escape!

302
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:01,140
[Yuru gasps]

303
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:07,650
[YAMAHA]
Hide in the world below!

304
00:17:07,690 --> 00:17:10,030
You mustn't let them find you!

305
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:11,200
[DERA] Aye, aye!

306
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:13,990
-[Kyoka grunts]
-Mom, are you all right?

307
00:17:14,030 --> 00:17:15,660
-[footsteps running]
-[Danji gasps]

308
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:17,410
[DANJI] Yuru?

309
00:17:17,450 --> 00:17:19,330
Yuru!

310
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:42,770
[Dera grunts]

311
00:17:42,810 --> 00:17:43,900
Let's go.

312
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:46,150
We're headed down
the mountain. Huh?

313
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:49,190
What kind of madness
is all this?

314
00:17:49,230 --> 00:17:51,070
Where did they come from?

315
00:17:51,110 --> 00:17:52,780
What's happening to our village?

316
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:55,240
-Save your questions!
-[gunshots]

317
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:06,250
Damn it, we missed our chance.

318
00:18:10,170 --> 00:18:13,760
And if those dentures come back,
the enemy will have us flanked.

319
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:15,300
-Asa.
-Huh?

320
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:19,310
I watched my sister
die back there. [cries]

321
00:18:19,810 --> 00:18:22,230
No, wait, is she dead?

322
00:18:22,270 --> 00:18:23,690
I thought I saw her move.

323
00:18:23,730 --> 00:18:26,730
But I left Granny
in a room with her.

324
00:18:26,770 --> 00:18:28,690
Who even was that woman?

325
00:18:29,230 --> 00:18:31,190
She said she'd kill them all.

326
00:18:31,230 --> 00:18:33,740
But none of the villagers
did anything to deserve it!

327
00:18:33,780 --> 00:18:34,780
[gunshots]

328
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:37,280
There's no time for me
to explain right now.

329
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:39,410
[Yuru breathing shakily]

330
00:18:40,490 --> 00:18:43,000
[DERA] Use them,
the Left and Right.

331
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:46,630
Huh? What do you mean?
It's a necklace.

332
00:18:47,130 --> 00:18:48,290
Over there.

333
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:51,920
There's a hole in the flagstones
between the Left and Right.

334
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:53,260
Put it there.

335
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:56,760
Mmm... And what do you think
that's gonna do?

336
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:59,470
Look, I'm givin' you
a gift, kid!

337
00:18:59,510 --> 00:19:00,640
Explain!

338
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:01,890
Just take it, already!

339
00:19:01,930 --> 00:19:05,270
It's gotta be you! Go on!

340
00:19:05,310 --> 00:19:08,150
What? Everyone's so crazy today!

341
00:19:08,190 --> 00:19:10,980
I just want answers.
Is that asking too much?

342
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:14,070
The hole's plugged up
with a bunch of junk!

343
00:19:14,110 --> 00:19:15,490
Dig it out!

344
00:19:16,150 --> 00:19:18,320
[COMBATANT]
That's the boy we're after.

345
00:19:18,370 --> 00:19:19,620
Capture him.

346
00:19:19,660 --> 00:19:20,990
Everyone else can die.

347
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:23,120
You really should clean up
around here!

348
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:24,500
[gunshot]

349
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:26,670
I got it. So now what?

350
00:19:30,130 --> 00:19:32,800
That hurt, Dera!
What was that about?

351
00:19:46,390 --> 00:19:47,770
[combatants grunting]

352
00:19:54,530 --> 00:19:56,110
[both scream]

353
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:01,410
What's going on?

354
00:20:01,490 --> 00:20:03,990
♪

355
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:29,640
[Yuru gasps]

356
00:20:29,690 --> 00:20:30,730
[Yuru grunts]

357
00:20:36,570 --> 00:20:39,450
[screams] No!

358
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:44,080
[GABBY] How am I supposed
to get back home now?

359
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:47,750
Walking down this mountain
is gonna suck bad.

360
00:20:47,790 --> 00:20:49,750
-[Gabriel grumbles]
-Yeah, yeah.

361
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:51,290
Quit your gnashing, you two.

362
00:20:51,330 --> 00:20:52,630
[Gabriel grumbles]

363
00:20:52,670 --> 00:20:54,750
Something big went that way.

364
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:57,880
Whose daemons are those?

365
00:20:58,760 --> 00:21:01,340
Hope they're not as strong
as they seemed.

366
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:06,890
[Yuru grunts]

367
00:21:09,430 --> 00:21:11,730
[Right laughs]
Whoa, what is this?

368
00:21:12,310 --> 00:21:15,230
Our new master is but a child.

369
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:18,610
Should be easy to control,
huh, Left?

370
00:21:18,650 --> 00:21:19,690
[Right laughs]

371
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:22,240
[LEFT] Young, old,
it matters not.

372
00:21:22,280 --> 00:21:23,950
-[Yuru gasps]
-[LEFT] We obey our master

373
00:21:23,990 --> 00:21:26,160
regardless, Right.

374
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:30,330
[DERA] Ghosts, spirits,

375
00:21:30,370 --> 00:21:33,500
monsters, aberrations,
cryptids...

376
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,460
They have many names.

377
00:21:35,500 --> 00:21:37,170
Hard for folks to know
what to call them

378
00:21:37,210 --> 00:21:39,010
when the only thing
consistent about them

379
00:21:39,050 --> 00:21:40,550
is they always come in pairs.

380
00:21:41,420 --> 00:21:44,890
Yuru, these are your Daemons.

381
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:52,890
Daemons?

382
00:21:56,150 --> 00:21:58,110
[♪ closing theme song playing]

383
00:23:26,650 --> 00:23:28,990
[MINE] The Left and Right's
bases at the village exit

384
00:23:29,030 --> 00:23:30,120
are directly above us.

385
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:31,790
Listen to me, Yuru.

386
00:23:31,830 --> 00:23:34,290
Know that no matter what happens
in the future,

387
00:23:34,330 --> 00:23:36,790
the Left and Right
are watching over you.

388
00:23:36,830 --> 00:23:39,920
EPISODE 2
LEFT AND RIGHT
